From da883ab753b0d6a01cc216c357204a2045ae6110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:57:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: sc2: retain VP9 references across capture
 changes

Separate a drained source-change CAPTURE stop from stream reset. Pin
stable FBC owners and private MV storage independently of vb2 objects,
and resolve inherited dimensions from the selected reference. Keep
normal seek, error invalidation and fatal DMA quarantine semantics.

Resolve show-existing headers against completed references rather
than waiting for a firmware header event that SC2 does not publish.
Only detached display references need a bounded compressed copy into
the current CAPTURE queue. Rebase populated scatter addresses while
preserving flags; do not relocate the original DPB or MV state.

Hardware series verification covers the complete original FATE stream,
two derived repeats, and existing P0/P2 size/depth/flush cases: 670
pictures and 110700144 samples exact, genuine EOF, and 5799936 bytes
of retained exports unchanged after close. Full image remains pending.

Change-Id: I2aabfcc21f16b807e34ada9ab0f2784d44c5ed47
